# Line-ending policy. Everything in this repo runs inside Linux containers, so
# LF is authoritative on every platform. Without this, a Windows checkout (git
# core.autocrlf) silently rewrites text files — including executable shell
# scripts — to CRLF, which then breaks when a Linux container executes them:
#   /docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/01-create-databases.sh: /bin/sh^M: bad interpreter
# Enforcing LF here prevents that for every future contributor, not just a
# one-time fix of the files affected today.

# Default: treat files as text with auto-detection, and always check out LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts are executed inside Linux containers — force LF explicitly,
# independent of the auto-detection above. This is the load-bearing line.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never line-ending-normalize (fonts live in app/fonts/).
*.woff2 binary
